sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as Web/Mobile Client
    participant Backend as Spring Boot Backend
    participant DB as PostgreSQL RDS
    participant S3 as AWS S3
    participant WS as WebSocket Service

    Note over Client,WS: 1. Initiate Batch Upload (Command)
    Client->>+Backend: POST /api/photos/batch-init<br/>{userId, photos: [metadata...]}
    Backend->>Backend: Create 100 Photo entities (PENDING)
    Backend->>+DB: Save all photos
    DB-->>-Backend: 100 records saved
    Backend->>Backend: Generate 100 presigned URLs
    Backend-->>-Client: {uploads: [{photoId, presignedUrl, s3Key}...]}

    Note over Client,WS: 2. Direct S3 Upload (Client → S3)
    loop For each photo (100 concurrent)
        Client->>Client: Track XHR progress (0-100%)
        Client->>+S3: PUT file to presigned URL
        Note over Client: Local progress: 23%
        
        alt Every 2 seconds (throttled)
            Client->>WS: WebSocket: {photoId, progress: 23%}
            WS-->>Client: Broadcast: {photoId, progress: 23%}
        end
        
        S3-->>-Client: Upload complete (HTTP 200)
    end

    Note over Client,WS: 3. Complete Upload Notification (Command)
    loop For each completed upload
        Client->>+Backend: POST /api/photos/{photoId}/complete<br/>{s3Key}
        Backend->>+S3: Verify object exists (HEAD request)
        S3-->>-Backend: Object exists: true
        Backend->>Backend: photo.markAsCompleted(s3Key)
        Backend->>+DB: Update photo status = COMPLETED
        DB-->>-Backend: Updated
        Backend->>WS: Notify completion
        WS-->>Client: WebSocket: {photoId, status: COMPLETED, progress: 100%}
        Backend-->>-Client: {status: COMPLETED, uploadedAt}
    end

    Note over Client,WS: 4. Query Photos (Query)
    Client->>+Backend: GET /api/photos?userId={id}&page=0&size=20
    Backend->>+DB: SELECT * FROM photos WHERE userId=?
    DB-->>-Backend: Page<Photo>
    Backend->>Backend: Generate download presigned URLs
    Backend-->>-Client: {photos: [{photoId, downloadUrl}...], pagination}
    
    Client->>+S3: GET download presigned URL
    S3-->>-Client: Image bytes
    Client->>Client: Display photo in gallery